# Tracking & Learning Loop

Always keep these three ledgers separate:

1. Model recommendation (version, scores, signal, time)
2. User action (buy/sell/bet/ignore, size, fees, venue)
3. Actual result (fill, settlement, PnL)

Crypto PnL includes trading fee, funding, gas, slippage, other costs.
Football PnL uses stake, odds, actual payout.
Lottery PnL uses ticket cost and prize.

Positions: multiple buys, add, reduce, full exit. Compute average cost, invested, current value, realized/unrealized/total PnL, ROI, holding time.

When a held asset is re-scanned, show current price, user cost, invested, value, floating PnL, ROI, original vs current model score, current signal, risk.

Model review records every prediction and computes win rate, profit factor, Sharpe, max DD, expectancy, precision, recall, calibration — then writes a new model version rather than overwriting.
